think The card's true unbuilt sibling: scale.rye (nearest-neighbor) is the only resize path, and it names "the area-average and bilinear paths grow beside it." Bilinear is the crux -- Lindy floor geometry read for years, the hardest-solvable clean move (a four-tap weighted blend in pure integer fixed-point), agent-doable with a witness on metal, no gate.
think Design: separable bilinear over color.mix (the palette family's linear lerp, t in 0..255 with /255 rounding). One per-axis map axis_sample yields a lower source index, an upper neighbor, and a weight; each pixel is three mixes. Center-aligned mapping in exact integers over 2*dst_extent so identity is byte-exact and both edges clamp. Compose not braid: no new color math, no codec, no premultiply.
obs One red caught and closed in-round: Zig 0.16 read the local name i0_u as a malformed primitive integer type (i + digit prefix, leading zero). Renamed the AxisSample fields and locals i0/i1 -> lo/hi; GREEN on the very next build. A machine caught it, not a second thought -- the reds-first pattern holds.
obs Bilinear's honest scope named plainly rather than overclaimed: it reads a 2x2 neighborhood, so a downscale far below half-size still aliases; the area-average path is that verb and grows next. Two Rooms discipline -- the smooth-interpolation floor is what this rung proves, not decimation.
loom witness=scale_bilinear_witness build_and_selftest=GREEN checks=8 identity_byte_exact=yes gradient_ascending=yes solid_stays_solid=yes alpha_blended=yes qoi_round_trip=byte_for_byte refusals=3 deterministic=yes
file image/scale_bilinear.rye the smooth resize: bilinear interpolation over color.mix + qoi buffers, integer-only, bounds up front, GREEN.
file tools/scale_bilinear_witness.rish proves it on metal with native `contains` (the REDS #85 loom), no fragile grep.
